WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.477
This is a first treatment for advanced cancer of the bile ducts

00:00:04.477 --> 00:00:08.445
or gallbladder. It combines chemotherapy and immunotherapy.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.720
Gemcitabine and cisplatin.

00:00:11.165 --> 00:00:16.965
These two chemotherapy medicines damage DNA or interrupt its copying as cells divide.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.932
Durvalumab, also called Imfinzi, is immunotherapy.

00:00:21.347 --> 00:00:26.157
Cancer cells can use a signal called PD-L1 to slow down immune cells.

00:00:26.577 --> 00:00:30.347
Durvalumab blocks that signal, helping immune cells attack cancer.

00:00:30.882 --> 00:00:31.749
TOPAZ-1.

00:00:32.194 --> 00:00:38.057
This trial tested whether adding durvalumab to chemotherapy helped people live longer.

00:00:38.437 --> 00:00:44.001
In a later analysis, about 12 in 100 people were alive at four years

00:00:44.001 --> 00:00:48.583
with durvalumab. About 4 in 100 were alive with placebo.

00:00:48.983 --> 00:00:50.563
These are group results.

00:00:51.003 --> 00:00:53.163
Your team can explain what they mean for you.

00:00:53.698 --> 00:00:54.512
Three weeks.

00:00:54.992 --> 00:00:56.982
Day 1. All three drugs.

00:00:57.462 --> 00:01:00.105
Day 8. Gemcitabine and cisplatin.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:06.479
Days 15 to 21 are a recovery week, without a scheduled anti-cancer drip.

00:01:06.479 --> 00:01:12.737
The next cycle starts three weeks after day 1, if your team says it is safe.

00:01:13.137 --> 00:01:16.101
A visit may move if you are unwell or need more tests,

00:01:16.101 --> 00:01:18.297
so use the date your day ward gives you.

00:01:18.797 --> 00:01:21.425
Durvalumab runs for about an hour,

00:01:21.425 --> 00:01:25.677
gemcitabine for half an hour and cisplatin for an hour.

00:01:26.057 --> 00:01:29.692
The drips total about two and a half hours. Fluids,

00:01:29.692 --> 00:01:33.754
anti-sickness medicines and checks make the visit longer.

00:01:34.214 --> 00:01:38.723
On day 8, gemcitabine is given first, followed by cisplatin.

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:41.503
There is no durvalumab on this visit.

00:01:41.883 --> 00:01:46.548
On both treatment days, you receive extra fluid before cisplatin

00:01:46.548 --> 00:01:51.213
to protect your kidneys. This can take another one to two hours.

00:01:51.613 --> 00:01:54.267
Allow extra time at the hospital for blood results,

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:56.973
assessment, preparation and any further observation.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:02:02.023
This time you receive just durvalumab, through a drip lasting about an hour.

00:02:02.463 --> 00:02:05.013
The plan repeats every four weeks while the treatment

00:02:05.013 --> 00:02:07.083
is helping and side effects are manageable.

00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:12.819
Blood tests check your blood cells and kidneys on both treatment days,

00:02:12.819 --> 00:02:18.953
and your liver on day 1. Your team also monitors blood sugar and thyroid function.

00:02:19.353 --> 00:02:23.173
At each visit, mention any new symptom, even if it has settled.

00:02:23.613 --> 00:02:26.733
It helps the team decide whether it is safe to give the next dose.

00:02:27.253 --> 00:02:30.393
A reaction can happen during a drip or shortly afterwards.

00:02:30.833 --> 00:02:34.844
Tell the nurse immediately if you feel hot, shivery, itchy or dizzy,

00:02:34.844 --> 00:02:38.443
or if your throat feels tight or breathing becomes difficult.

00:02:38.853 --> 00:02:42.493
Staff can pause the infusion, check you and treat the reaction.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:49.442
Nausea, vomiting, tiredness and a sore mouth can happen. Your team can help treat them.

00:02:49.822 --> 00:02:53.662
Follow your team’s fluid advice for the first 24 hours

00:02:53.662 --> 00:02:57.927
after cisplatin, especially if you have a fluid restriction.

00:02:58.307 --> 00:03:04.372
Ring urgently if you cannot keep fluids down or mouth ulcers stop you drinking.

00:03:04.852 --> 00:03:08.285
If you develop a fever or suddenly feel unwell, ring the 24-hour

00:03:08.285 --> 00:03:11.612
number straight away so the team can also check for infection.

00:03:12.032 --> 00:03:16.316
Ring immediately if your temperature is 37.5°C or higher,

00:03:16.316 --> 00:03:22.178
or 36°C or lower. Ring if you feel suddenly unwell even with a normal reading.

00:03:22.558 --> 00:03:26.179
Low platelets can cause easy bruising or bleeding.

00:03:26.179 --> 00:03:29.438
Tell your team about new bruises or bleeding.

00:03:29.898 --> 00:03:33.377
Ring your oncology team urgently for new fever,

00:03:33.377 --> 00:03:37.595
shaking chills, yellow skin or eyes, or upper tummy pain.

00:03:37.975 --> 00:03:41.617
Tell them if you have a bile duct stent.

00:03:41.617 --> 00:03:46.897
Do not wait for all these symptoms or for your next visit.

00:03:47.377 --> 00:03:51.947
Passing much less urine than usual or developing new swelling is another reason to ring.

00:03:52.342 --> 00:03:56.977
Cisplatin can affect hearing and nerves. Tell your team promptly

00:03:56.977 --> 00:03:59.946
about ringing in your ears, hearing loss,

00:03:59.946 --> 00:04:03.712
or new tingling or numbness in your fingers or toes.

00:04:04.192 --> 00:04:07.182
Sometimes the immune system inflames healthy organs too.

00:04:07.622 --> 00:04:11.362
A new cough or shortness of breath may be a sign of lung inflammation.

00:04:11.802 --> 00:04:14.882
Ring your oncology team urgently, even between visits.

00:04:15.322 --> 00:04:18.762
For the bowel, ring about new diarrhoea, even if mild.

00:04:19.202 --> 00:04:23.722
Tell the team how often you are going and whether there is pain, blood or mucus.

00:04:24.162 --> 00:04:28.522
Blisters, peeling skin or painful mouth sores need urgent assessment.

00:04:28.962 --> 00:04:32.322
Side effects can first appear months after your last infusion.

00:04:32.842 --> 00:04:37.062
Before you leave the day ward, save your hospital’s 24-hour oncology number.

00:04:37.502 --> 00:04:42.462
Carry your immunotherapy alert card and show it if you see a GP or an emergency team.

00:04:42.902 --> 00:04:47.222
If you feel unwell and cannot reach oncology, seek urgent medical assessment.

00:04:47.657 --> 00:04:54.062
For severe breathing difficulty, severe chest pain or collapse, call 112 or 999.
